## 5. Secure audio URL ingestion (must-pass requirements)

Public server-side URL fetching creates SSRF exposure. Implement the URL endpoint as a **restricted fetcher**, never use a naive `httpx.get(user_url)` / `requests.get(user_url)` implementation.

1. `URL_FETCH_ENABLED=true|false`; **default false** until an allowed host list has been configured. The service can expose the endpoint but reject URL requests if disabled.
2. `ALLOWED_AUDIO_HOSTS=media.example.org,*.trusted-storage.example.com` and **no wildcard-all** mode in production. Hostname matching must be exact or dot-boundary-safe (not suffix substring).
3. Only `https` and standard permitted TCP ports (default 443); reject userinfo, fragments, IP literals, malformed internationalized hostnames, encoded control characters, and ambiguous URL syntax.
4. Resolve all A/AAAA records and reject loopback, RFC1918/private, link-local, multicast, reserved, unspecified, IPv4-mapped IPv6 and other non-globally-routable targets. If any address is disallowed, fail closed.
5. Prevent DNS rebinding / TOCTOU: connection must be made to an already validated IP while preserving the approved hostname for TLS SNI and certificate validation; alternatively enforce an egress proxy/firewall that only permits explicitly approved external destinations and document its verification. **A DNS check followed by an ordinary hostname connection is not sufficient.**
6. `follow_redirects=False`, including redirects to an otherwise permitted URL, until each redirect hop can be independently revalidated/pinned. Simplest v1: reject 3xx.
7. Disable environment-derived HTTP proxies (`trust_env=False`) unless explicitly administered and audited; never send credentials or auth headers to arbitrary remote origins.
8. Set connect/read/total download timeouts (e.g. 5/15/20 seconds), stream with a 20 MiB cap, cap decompressed/decoded output, validate HTTP status and real audio format. Reject responses claiming unlimited streams.
9. Signed URLs: accept query strings for the authorized host but **redact them** from logs, traces and error responses; do not store them in exceptions. Ensure URL is not reflected back to caller.
10. Add hardening at deployment: default no outbound access except allowlisted storage domains (network proxy/firewall) when possible; no credentials exposed in URL.

**Minimum URL security tests**: `127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, `10.0.0.1`, `169.254.169.254`, `[::1]`, `[::ffff:127.0.0.1]`, private DNS answer, mixed public/private DNS answers, DNS rebinding, redirect to private IP, `http://`, `https://good.example.evil.org`, URL userinfo, oversized chunk stream, endless slow stream, invalid MIME and wrong decoded format. Mock DNS and transport; **do not** make real external requests in fast CI.

