## 6. Authentication, limits and observability

- Use optional `X-API-Key` for private network deployment; when enabled, compare with constant-time comparison and avoid logging the value. Set `REQUIRE_API_KEY=true` by default for externally reachable deployments.
- Support rotation via redeploy or documented secret management; keep keys in `.env`/Docker secrets, never commit keys.
- Respect `X-Request-ID` only after sanitization, otherwise generate a unique request ID.
- Rate limiting and body size enforcement should be applied **also at Traefik/Nginx**, not only inside the app.
- Structured logs: request ID, endpoint, status, duration, model version, source kind (upload/url), score reliability boolean; no raw audio, expected sentence or signed URL.
- Recommended metrics (if added later): request totals/errors, p50/p95 latency, CPU inference wait time, model readiness, URL download failures. No Prometheus dependency required in v1.
- Configure CORS explicitly; no `*` for public authenticated browser clients.
- Always clean temp artifacts. Handle Ctrl+C / SIGTERM / graceful shutdown.

