## 10. Model versioning and operational concerns

- Start with `openpronounce==1.1.0`, then lock transitive versions; release test and runtime must share the same dependency lock.
- Record model IDs, exact Hugging Face revisions and checksums where upstream allows. If upstream source does not expose a reproducible model revision, document the gap and snapshot/cache known artifacts for the image.
- Avoid automatic model updates at container startup in production.
- Expose model readiness separately from liveness. Cold start may be substantial; enable proper start period for health checks.
- One worker by default to avoid multiplying resident model memory; tune `OMP_NUM_THREADS` / `TORCH_NUM_THREADS` and maximum concurrency empirically on the target CPU.
- Size memory based on measurements: upstream suggests ~4 GiB per instance; 8 GiB host with other services needs headroom.
- Do not claim native-like score or pronunciation correctness. Score is a model estimate and depends on length, child vs adult voices, accent and recording quality.
- For short words, a single altered sound can dominate score; present cautious feedback and never treat score as identity or ability assessment.

