## 13. Definition of Done / acceptance criteria

- [ ] Python runtime is 3.12 and dependency resolution is reproducible with a committed lockfile.
- [ ] `POST /api/v1/assess` assesses a provided audio file against an English word, phrase or sentence.
- [ ] `POST /api/v1/assess/url` downloads an **allowlisted HTTPS** audio resource with SSRF defenses and returns the same response schema.
- [ ] Both paths invoke OpenPronounce with `acoustic=False`, `prosody=False`, `transcription=True` (no TTS/network synthesis).
- [ ] Real upstream output is mapped without inventing error/phoneme/score fields; `reliable=false` is displayed as `uncertain`, not pass/fail.
- [ ] Audio bytes/duration/formats validated; temporary files removed in all paths; errors use stable JSON shape.
- [ ] URL endpoint rejects private/loopback/rebound DNS targets, redirects, prohibited schemes and oversized/slow streams.
- [ ] API-key authentication configurable; logs never expose raw audio, API key or signed URL.
- [ ] Fast unit/API/security tests work without downloading multi-GB models; `scripts/test.sh` passes locally and in CI.
- [ ] `scripts/test-api.sh` and `scripts/test-model.sh` exist, are executable, and have documented prerequisites.
- [ ] Docker Compose starts CPU-only service as non-root, with correctly gated readiness and model loading.
- [ ] Tagged GitHub release runs all mandatory checks and publishes a versioned GHCR image **only after** full-model smoke and license verification.
- [ ] README documents exact setup, configuration, upload and URL usage, tests, offline operation and known limitations.
- [ ] Project licensing decisions and redistributable model artifacts are documented and approved before public publication.

